<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 11.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 10/11/96  10/04/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    210.35    205.15    90.46	88.22     93.30</p>
<p>West	    234.67    232.95    88.78	88.33     92.10</p>
<p>Total Canada  445.02    438.10    89.56	83.27     92.20</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 10/11/96: 232.31 bcf, 10/04/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 10/11/96: 264.34 bcf, 10/04/96: 263.74 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
